# T-216 Part 2 — the daily recurring-expense drafting run. INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS: docs/ops/README.md
#
# ⛔ IT DRAFTS. IT NEVER PAYS. v1 auto-pays a due recurring expense on a cron — posts the expense
# and moves real cash. Ian, 6–7 Sep 2026: v2 does not. This creates a PENDING supplier invoice and a
# DRAFT expense and stops. Nothing reaches the ledger until a person has read the real bill,
# attached it, verified the invoice and approved the expense.
#
# ⭐ It acts as each template's CREATOR through the ordinary authorization gates, not as a system
# principal — so the automation can never do what the person who set it up could not. A creator who
# has since lost store scope produces a loud per-template failure, which is the right failure.
#
# ⚠️ What it does NOT need: a receipt. The machine has none, and `verifyInvoice` refuses an invoice
# without one — which is the gate working, not a problem to solve here.

[Unit]
Description=Shareat — draft today's due recurring expenses (T-216)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target
# No After=postgresql.service — the database is DO Managed Postgres, off-box (ADR-002 §1).

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/srv/shareat
ExecStart=/usr/bin/npm run recurring-expense-draft
User=shareat
Group=shareat

# ⚠️ NEVER build here. This is a small droplet; a build OOMs it. This unit runs an already-installed
# tree shipped by CI — bible §2.10.
Environment=NODE_ENV=production

# ⭐ The exit code is load-bearing: non-zero when anything failed, so the host's mailer speaks up.
# ⛔ A template with no supplier prints here as a named failure. It is the commonest one, it is a
# configuration fault rather than a bug, and the fix is one field on /expenses/recurring.
StandardOutput=append:/var/log/shareat/recurring-expense-draft.log
StandardError=append:/var/log/shareat/recurring-expense-draft.log
